<!-- Content sections -->
<section class="section-parchment section-pad">
  <div class="page-container">
    <div class="model-pillars">

      <!-- Conventions -->
      <div id="conventions">
        <div class="pillar-head">
          <span class="tone-accent">{{ kiIcon("compass", 28) }}</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="pillar-title">Conventions</h2>
            <p class="caption-md">The shared language that makes an island coherent — and interoperable with others.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-ki pillar-intro">
          <p>Conventions are what allow an island to be understood by anyone operating within it — including its own future agents. They define how knowledge is expressed, where it lives, and what belongs on the island at all.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-3col grid-gap-1">
          <div class="card-ki">
            <h3 class="card-heading">Notes</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Format and type system: frontmatter, tags, note types, structural conventions for both machine and human readability. The grammar of knowledge on the island.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-ki">
            <h3 class="card-heading">Residency</h3>
            <p class="card-text">What belongs on the island versus in external systems. The boundary between a Knowledge Island and the tools it uses is a convention decision — and it must be deliberate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-ki">
            <h3 class="card-heading">Structure</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Library layout: the four zones (Calendar, Pillars, Resources), routing rules for incoming knowledge, index conventions, folder naming. The map of the island.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Processes -->
      <div id="processes">
        <div class="pillar-head">
          <span class="tone-accent">{{ kiIcon("lighthouse", 28) }}</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="pillar-title">Processes</h2>
            <p class="caption-md">The formal gates that govern how the island changes — and how it relates to the outside world.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-ki pillar-intro">
          <p>Processes are what give governance its teeth. Without them, conventions are aspirational and decisions are informal. Processes make change legible, traceable, and ratifiable.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2col grid-gap-1-5">
          <div class="process-card">
            <div class="process-head">
              <span class="process-icon process-icon-accent">{{ kiIcon("lighthouse", 20) }}</span>
              <h3 class="process-title">Enactment Process</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="process-text">The internal change mechanism. Any update to the island's conventions, structure, or governance flows through here: draft → council review → ratification.</p>
            <p class="process-note">How the island governs itself.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="process-card">
            <div class="process-head">
              <span class="process-icon process-icon-teal">{{ kiIcon("harbour", 20) }}</span>
              <h3 class="process-title">Contribution Process</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="process-text">External propagation — how an island proposes additions or changes to the shared Knowledge Islands model. How individual islands contribute to the archipelago.</p>
            <p class="process-note">How the island governs the commons.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Activities -->
      <div id="activities">
        <div class="pillar-head">
          <span class="tone-ok">{{ kiIcon("tree", 28) }}</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="pillar-title">Activities</h2>
            <p class="caption-md">The ongoing work that keeps an island alive — scheduled and conversational, required and optional.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-ki pillar-intro">
          <p>An island that stops running its activities stops being a Knowledge Island. It becomes an archive. Activities are the tending — the regular, deliberate work of keeping knowledge current, healthy, and trustworthy.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2col grid-gap-1-5">

          <div>
            <p class="label-caps activity-label activity-label-accent">Constitutional</p>
            <div class="activity-stack">
              <div class="activity-item">
                <p class="activity-name">Conformance</p>
                <p class="caption-sm">Verifies baseline conventions and adoption decisions. Non-negotiable — the island must be able to verify it is what it claims to be.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="label-caps activity-label activity-label-ok">Tending</p>
            <div class="activity-stack activity-stack-tight">
              <div class="activity-item activity-item-sm">
                <p class="activity-name activity-name-sm">Audit · Health Check · Knowledge Rebuild</p>
                <p class="caption-xs">Scheduled — run on a cadence</p>
              </div>
              <div class="activity-item activity-item-sm">
                <p class="activity-name activity-name-sm">Inbox Review · Asset Audit · Status Review</p>
                <p class="caption-xs">Conversational — judgment-heavy</p>
              </div>
              <div class="activity-item activity-item-sm">
                <p class="activity-name activity-name-sm">Structural Audit · Wikilink Review · Convergence Check</p>
                <p class="caption-xs">Deep — periodic structural review</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="label-caps activity-label activity-label-teal">Briefings</p>
            <div class="activity-item">
              <p class="activity-name">Morning Briefing</p>
              <p class="caption-sm">Daily preparation: calendar review, task orientation, inbox state. Sets the agent in context for the day's work.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="label-caps activity-label activity-label-warn">Integration</p>
            <div class="activity-stack activity-stack-tight">
              <div class="activity-item activity-item-sm">
                <p class="activity-name activity-name-sm">Email Management</p>
                <p class="caption-xs">Inbox triage with knowledge-aware routing</p>
              </div>
              <div class="activity-item activity-item-sm">
                <p class="activity-name activity-name-sm">Linear</p>
                <p class="caption-xs">Project workspace aligned with island governance</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Agents -->
      <div id="agents">
        <div class="pillar-head">
          <span class="tone-teal">{{ kiIcon("route", 28) }}</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="pillar-title">Agents</h2>
            <p class="caption-md">The operating patterns for each kind of agent — human and artificial.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-ki pillar-intro">
          <p>The model defines operating conventions for each agent type — not just what they can do, but how they should behave, what constraints they operate under, and what authority they hold. The same island can be operated by different agents at different times, consistently.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-3col grid-gap-1">
          <div class="card-ki">
            <p class="heading-display agent-role">Human</p>
            <p class="card-text">Full island membership. Ratification authority. Operates through editor interfaces and conversational AI. Source of meaning and values.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-ki">
            <p class="heading-display agent-role">Claude</p>
            <p class="card-text">Primary AI agent. Accesses the island via MCP. Runs activities, assists with connection and curation, participates in governance drafting. Does not ratify.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-ki">
            <p class="heading-display agent-role">ChatGPT</p>
            <p class="card-text">Secondary AI agent. Different capability profile; complementary role. Operates under equivalent constraints to Claude — island-specific operating instructions govern both.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tools -->
      <div id="tools">
        <div class="pillar-head">
          <span class="tone-accent">{{ kiIcon("anchor", 28) }}</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="pillar-title">Tools</h2>
            <p class="caption-md">The instruments through which agents operate — the technology layer that the model runs on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-ki pillar-intro">
          <p>The model is portable — it doesn't require specific tools. But the reference implementation (Arcadia) runs on a defined stack, which shapes the conventions and activities described above.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-grid">
          <div class="tool-tile">
            <p class="icon-row tone-accent">{{ kiIcon("book", 24) }}</p>
            <p class="heading-display tool-name">Obsidian</p>
            <p class="caption-xs">Primary note editor; human interface to the Library</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-tile">
            <p class="icon-row tone-accent">{{ kiIcon("stellar", 24) }}</p>
            <p class="heading-display tool-name">Claude</p>
            <p class="caption-xs">Primary AI — activities, curation, drafting</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-tile">
            <p class="icon-row tone-teal">{{ kiIcon("weave", 24) }}</p>
            <p class="heading-display tool-name">ChatGPT</p>
            <p class="caption-xs">Secondary AI — complementary perspective</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-tile">
            <p class="icon-row tone-accent">{{ kiIcon("grid", 24) }}</p>
            <p class="heading-display tool-name">Linear</p>
            <p class="caption-xs">Project management aligned with governance</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-tile">
            <p class="icon-row tone-accent">{{ kiIcon("current", 24) }}</p>
            <p class="heading-display tool-name">Microsoft 365</p>
            <p class="caption-xs">Communication and calendar integration</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Arcadia callout -->
      <div class="night-callout">
        <p class="overline-gold">The Living Instance</p>
        <h3 class="heading-display-light night-callout-title">Arcadia implements every part of this model.</h3>
        <p class="night-callout-text">
          From conventions and governance to activities and agent operating patterns — Arcadia is the canonical reference implementation. The model is not aspirational. It is working.
        </p>
        <a href="/philosophy/" class="btn-ghost-light">← Back to Philosophy</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
